# Connection string for a WRITE account — loading does INSERTs, so a read-only account cannot do it.
#  ★ The account you give SoriTrading is the other one: a READ-ONLY account (readonly_bot).
#  ★ .env is gitignored. This file is only an example and holds no secret.
#
#  Supabase direct:  postgres://postgres:PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
#  Supabase pooler:  postgres://postgres.<project-ref>:PASSWORD@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres

# ── Optional: realtime wake-up over Redis ────────────────────────────────────
#  After inserting new rows the loader publishes "something new arrived" so a strategy
#  agent can re-read immediately instead of waiting for its next poll.
#  ★ This is OPTIONAL. Without it the data is exactly as correct — only slower to arrive.
#  ★ The publisher and the subscriber must reach the SAME Redis. On one machine that is
#    simply redis://127.0.0.1:6379; across machines see the guide linked in the README.
#  ★ Values never travel through Redis — only the signal. Missing one is harmless because
#    the next poll catches up.
# SORI_WAKE_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
